{
  "schema": "northstar-stage3-native-write-results-v1",
  "status": "PassedLimitedNativeWriteAndAckKnowledgeSlice",
  "scope": [
    "Receiving TCP/WS callbacks create an invocation-local owner before polling their prepare/write/settle child. The same borrowed OutboundItem, stanza and receipt channels survive through that child; retirement follows child destruction, including caught panic.",
    "The production lease supplies its bound stanza to the real writer helper. It records actual full-write/failure separately from the permission decision, then issues a private consuming written continuation. Dropping that continuation never acknowledges.",
    "Existing TCP write_all/flush and WS cancellation priority/timeout behavior are retained. Full local write is recorded before transport notifications and ACK await; it is not peer receipt.",
    "Native ACK requests bind the exact returned fence and operation. Actual C2S/MIX SQL commit sites retain unconfirmed COMMIT-entry and synchronous positive receipt before returning. Checked C2S deletion, allowed absent-unclaimed and MIX committed no-match are different facts.",
    "C2S initial message-ID claims rotate, non-initial claims stay exact and returned claims are Some. MIX token inequality is not invented. Existing SM ownership suppresses native fence/ACK; no new read, retry, reconciliation consumer or deadline is added."
  ],
